      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5b75f0d44d4a8d6deed70bd3|full_name}: I think there's a gradient here.\nThere's some people who, if given a unitypackage file, wouldn't be capable of installing the right version of Unity, VRCSDK, importing the package and uploading it. For those people, it would be nice if you could just send them a file which VRChat itself would just import without the need for Unity. It would of course be nice if this file were also usable as asset data for people who did know what they were doing.\nObviously VRM was already indicated as one potential format for this, as it's already in use between several applications for this purpose, but VRChat has its things that it supports that VRM does not, so they'd have to have their own extensions.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
