      "restoredAt": null,
      "sourceFeatureExtractionItemID": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{627e94e69bf04e1ede28a21b|full_name} Howdy, I orignally posted this before the canny wipe. Can We get an update for this? \n\nThe new marketplace system has a nice system for updating avatars and being able to send clients a redeemable code for an avatar commission seems possible now with the code redemption systems from last year. \n\nMarking the avatar as \"Unlisted\" on a marketplace backend but able to be redeemed via code is a nice secure way to distribute commissions and also other types of promotional avatars. This system can also follow normal marketplace rules and safeguards such as protections for the client like avatar update approvals and other. \n\nHopefully this canny gets dusted off and reduced the need for distributing logins and mixing up Hardware IDs between accounts",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
